172:## Interactive Server/Web Terminal Backends
195:The non-interactive agent `run_bash` path does not use this backend.
211:Representative interactive backend tests:
223:- **Linux/macOS**: `run_bash` uses a non-interactive POSIX shell process.
224:- **Windows**: `run_bash` executes through WSL with non-interactive `bash`; WSL/tmux remains an interactive terminal backend concern.
225:- **Android**: command execution uses a non-interactive shell available in the Termux environment.
227:For server/web interactive terminals, `node-pty` remains relevant to PTY-backed sessions. On macOS it runs inside the isolated helper-process backend; on other Unix-like systems it can run in the parent-process `PtySession` backend. It is not part of stateless agent `run_bash`.
